The Venus vTHE market combined two flaws. First, six EOAs (including the victim) had pre-approved the future attack-contract address to spend their THE; the attacker used those standing allowances to pull ~36M THE and donate it directly into the vTHE contract. A direct token donation into a Compound-fork money market is not booked through `mint`, so it silently inflates the market's cash / exchange rate and therefore the value of the victim's vTHE collateral. Second, Venus's `borrowBehalf(borrower, amount)` lets a third party open debt on another account's behalf without that account's authorization. With the victim's collateral artificially over-valued by the donation, the attacker called `borrowBehalf(VICTIM, ...)` to borrow USDC, CAKE and WBNB against the victim while receiving the cash itself, then minted vUSDC and re-borrowed/re-donated THE to keep the collateral inflated. The result: debt piled onto the victim, real assets (CAKE + WBNB) extracted to the attacker.

**Vulnerable code snippet:**

```solidity
// donation directly inflates vTHE cash / exchange rate (not via mint)
THE.transferFrom(donorEOA, address(VTHE), amount);
// borrowBehalf opens debt on the victim, cash goes to caller
VUSDC.borrowBehalf(VICTIM, USDC_BORROW_AMOUNT);
VCAKE.borrowBehalf(VICTIM, CAKE_BORROW_AMOUNT);
VWBNB.borrowBehalf(VICTIM, WBNB_BORROW_AMOUNT);
```

