[https://blog.verichains.io/p/vulnerability-analysis-deconstructing](https://blog.verichains.io/p/vulnerability-analysis-deconstructing)

KRC is a fee-on-transfer (deflationary) token. The attacker exploited the interaction between its transfer fee/burn and the PancakeSwap pair's `skim` function to desynchronize the pair's cached reserves from its real token balances. With nested DODO and PancakeV3 flashloans of USDT, the attacker first swapped USDT into KRC to set up an imbalance, then performed a sequence of ~17 precise `transfer(pair, amount)` followed by `pair.skim(this)` calls. Because the deflationary token burns/taxes on each transfer, repeatedly sending KRC into the pair and skimming caused the pair's internal reserves to drift away from actual balances, lowering the effective KRC price. The attacker then executed a single `pair.swap(0, 355361...)` to extract a large amount of USDT against the corrupted reserves, repaid both flashloans, and netted ~$7k. Root cause: AMM pair reserve accounting being manipulable through a deflationary token's transfer fee combined with `skim`.

**Vulnerable code snippet:**

```solidity
// repeat ~17x: deflationary transfer into pair then skim desyncs reserves
krcToken.transfer(address(krc_pair), 26158607120271760914);
krc_pair.skim(address(this));
... // 16 more transfer+skim rounds with decreasing amounts
// then extract USDT against the corrupted reserves
krc_pair.swap(0, 355361934507515425212391, address(this), new bytes(0));
```

